cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LingCoT: Linguistic Corpus Toolkit"
message: "If LingCoT contributes to published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Serova
    given-names: Kutay
repository-code: "https://github.com/kutay-serova/LingCoT"
abstract: >-
  A desktop tool for annotating linguistic corpora: interlinear glossing from
  document down to morpheme following the Leipzig Glossing Rules, a dictionary
  that grows with the corpus, manual dependency parsing in a CoNLL-U-compatible
  schema, concordance search, and per-field annotator provenance. Built for
  language documentation. Runs offline, stores corpora as plain-text JSONL, and
  keeps fieldwork data outside the application folder.
keywords:
  - linguistics
  - language documentation
  - interlinear glossing
  - corpus annotation
  - Leipzig Glossing Rules
  - lexicography
  - fieldwork
license: MIT
